  "final_message": "The bug was in `paginate()`: pages are numbered from 1, but it calculated the start index as `page * page_size`, so every page came back one page too late (page 1 gave `[3, 4]` instead of `[1, 2]`). I changed it to `(page - 1) * page_size` in `paginate.py:8`, which is the same formula `page_bounds` already uses.\n\n`python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` now passes; there is only one test. That was the only line I changed; `total_pages` and `page_bounds` are untouched.\n\nDONE: Fixed an off-by-one in paginate() so the start index is (page - 1) * page_size; the public test passes.",
